    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕtaxa</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mătaxa</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέταξα</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάταξα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>raw silk</i>, the web of silkworms. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 39,
				4, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11, 7,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a rope</i>: lini
			metaxa, Lucil. ap. Fest. s. v. rodus, p. 265 Müll.; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7,
			3</span></i>.</div>
